{q:`Which exam domain has the highest weight?`,o:[`Troubleshooting & Optimization`,`Output Evaluation & Validation`,`Product & Model Selection`,`Configuration & Knowledge Management`],r:1,a:`<p><b>Output Evaluation &amp; Validation</b>, at 21%.</p>`},
{q:`How many questions and how much time does the exam have (guide v1.0)?`,a:`<p><b>60 questions</b> in <b>120 minutes</b>. The pass mark is <b>720 out of 1,000</b>.</p>`},
{q:`In scenario questions, which answer is usually best?`,o:[`The most technical one`,`The safest, most practical one that solves the real problem`,`The longest one`,`The one that uses the biggest model`],r:1,a:`<p>The exam tests <b>judgement</b>: practical, safe and proportionate choices.</p>`},
{q:`Name the 7 skills in order, in one word each.`,a:`<p><b>Set up, Ask, Check, Design, Configure, Govern, Fix.</b></p>`},
{q:`What are the 5 steps for answering a scenario question?`,a:`<p><b>Read what is asked, find the real problem, name the domain, remove clearly wrong answers, choose the safest practical fix.</b></p>`},
{q:`A question says "Select TWO". What is the best approach?`,o:[`Pick the two longest answers`,`Judge each option as true or false on its own, then pick exactly two`,`Pick three to be safe`,`Pick only one`],r:1,a:`<p>Judge each option separately and pick <b>exactly the number asked</b>.</p>`}
